Hello,

there is no automated way for using several input matrices in monmonier. You'll have to run several algorithms, one per matrix, or merge all your matrices into one e.g. by averaging your matrices possibly with after a standardization. It really depends on the question you ask to your data.

You can export triangular matrices in R (using cat and a bit of coding - that would be a question for R-help), but if you don't especially need triangular matrices for another software, then it's much simpler to export a square matrix.

Cheers

Thibaut.
